{"workspace_id":"0745b727-7577-463c-a2bc-3f85582e7a05","revision":2,"source":"synthetic:cedar/02-signed-trial-readings.md","title":"02-signed-trial-readings.md","id":"cedar-2","text":"# Cedar cold-room retrofit: signed C-21 measurements\nDocument status: signed final. Scope: the same 24-hour load profile in controlled trial C-21.\nSynthetic local data; not public-source evidence or production measurements.\nBaseline consumed 240 kWh. Dune consumed 208 kWh; its maximum interior temperature was 5.2 degrees Celsius and its average temperature was 4.1 degrees Celsius. Reed consumed 210 kWh; its maximum interior temperature was 5.0 degrees Celsius and its average temperature was 4.3 degrees Celsius.\nThe trial used the same duration, ambient-temperature profile, and cooling load for all three runs. There were no missing temperature samples. These are the final C-21 readings.\n","version":2}